Hi Jacqueline,

Thank you for joining the shift briefing today. I have attached version 2.0 o=
f the handover sheet. Please replace the old sheet wherever it is distributed=
 to the shift team, starting with the 17:30 JST handover today. We will do th=
e same for the Japan shift.

The sheet separates the person to check with in Japan and the source from the=
 next customer update: its date and time in JST, the person who will contact =
the customer, and the message. If the Japan contact or the next customer upda=
te is blank, please return the sheet to the Japan shift for confirmation. Ple=
ase do not infer the customer update time from the deadline for an internal i=
nquiry. If an answer is still pending, the customer contact owner should stil=
l give the agreed progress update at the stated time.

Tomorrow morning, Hara, you and I will read back the first 12 cases from toda=
y's 17:30 handover together. Let's check whether both shifts can identify the=
 Japan contact, the customer contact owner and the next update time. The new =
entry guide also shows how to record an update when the technical answer is p=
ending.

Thanks,
Yumika

